            <ArticleTitle>[Primary non-polipoid intestinal folicular lymphoma: case report and review of the literature].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>85-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The primary intestinal follicular lymphoma is a rare disease described in the last classification of lymphomas from WHO. It is a localized disease with excellent prognosis. We describe in this article ,a 64 year-old Peruvian female with abdominal pain and delayed vomiting for the last two years, has undergone a partial intestinal resection due to bowel obstruction. There was a well-circumscribed annular tumor. A diagnosis of non-polypoid primary intestinal follicular lymphoma was made. We report the case and review the literature in this article.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
